@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+---
+name: polli
+description: Route requests through Pollinations models.
+managed_by: polli
+---
+
+# Polli
+
+You may use the **Pollinations** provider (`id: pollinations`) for any
+text-generation request. It is registered as an `openai-compatible`
+provider in this Prime installation, so you can call it the same way
+you would any other chat-completions endpoint.
+
+## When to use
+
+* The user explicitly asks for a Pollinations model.
+* The user says "use polli" / "use pollinations" / "use the polli model".
+* A cheaper or open model is preferred and Pollinations serves one.
+
+## Selecting a model
+
+The currently configured default is whatever `polli harness prime status`
+reports. To switch the default for *future* sessions, run:
+
+```sh
+polli harness prime on --default-model <id>
+```
+
+You can also request a specific model inline if the request includes
+one ("use mistral"). Available ids are listed by `polli harness prime
+status`.
+
+## Auth
+
+The provider is authenticated with a Pollinations API key scoped to
+`prime-agent`. It is separate from any other Pollinations keys you may
+hold and can be rotated without affecting them:
+
+```sh
+polli login --scope prime-agent --rotate
+```
+
+After rotating, re-run `polli harness prime on` to refresh the
+descriptor in Prime.
+
+## Disconnecting
+
+To stop using Pollinations from Prime without affecting any other
+Prime state:
+
+```sh
+polli harness prime off
+```
+
+This removes the `pollinations` provider entry and this skill file,
+and rotates the dedicated key. Your sessions, memories, other skills,
+and unrelated config are left untouched.
