@@ -0,0 +1,196 @@
+# Pollinations <-> Prime Agent
+
+This guide explains, from a user's perspective, how to set up, inspect,
+select models for, and remove the Pollinations integration with
+[Prime Agent](https://github.com/PrimeAgent/prime).
+
+The integration is **non-destructive**: it adds a custom provider and a
+single skill to your existing Prime installation. Your sessions,
+memories, other skills, and unrelated configuration are preserved at
+every step.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Prerequisites
+
+* A working `polli` CLI, authenticated via `polli login`.
+* Either an existing Prime Agent installation, or a willingness to
+  install one. `polli harness prime on` will detect a missing install
+  and point you at the official setup.
+
+## 2. Setup
+
+### 2.1 Issue a dedicated key for Prime
+
+```sh
+polli login --for-prime
+```
+
+This issues (or rotates) a Pollinations API key tagged with the
+`prime-agent` scope. The scope is **separate** from any other
+Pollinations keys you hold, so rotating or revoking it has no effect
+on unrelated clients.
+
+### 2.2 Turn the integration on
+
+```sh
+polli harness prime on
+```
+
+What this does:
+
+1. Locates your Prime home (`$PRIME_HOME`, defaulting to `~/.prime`).
+2. Takes a timestamped backup of `providers.json` and `skills/` into
+   `$PRIME_HOME/.backups/polli-<ts>/`.
+3. Adds a `pollinations` entry to `providers.json` (an
+   OpenAI-compatible provider pointing at Pollinations).
+4. Writes a `skills/polli.md` file describing when/how to use the
+   provider.
+
+If you have an existing `polli.md` skill that you have customised and
+don't want overwritten, pass `--keep-skill`:
+
+```sh
+polli harness prime on --keep-skill
+```
+
+The command is **idempotent**: running it twice leaves the same
+on-disk state.
+
+## 3. Inspecting status
+
+```sh
+polli harness prime status
+```
+
+Reports:
+
+* Whether the integration is installed (provider + skill both present).
+* The Prime home it is acting on.
+* The currently selected default model.
+* The list of currently compatible Pollinations models.
+
+`polli status` (the global one) also includes a short Prime section,
+so you can check readiness in one place.
+
+Exit codes are scriptable:
+
* `0` - installed and ready
* `1` - not installed but Prime is present
* `2` - Prime Agent itself is missing
+
+## 4. Selecting a model
+
+To list currently compatible Pollinations models:
+
+```sh
+polli harness prime models
+```
+
+To set the default model used for **future** Prime sessions:
+
+```sh
+polli harness prime on --default-model mistral
+```
+
+The model list is maintained in the integration; new Pollinations
+models become available as soon as they're added there.
+
+## 5. Rotating the key
+
+```sh
+polli login --for-prime
+```
+
+This rotates the `prime-agent`-scoped key. After rotating, re-run:
+
+```sh
+polli harness prime on
+```
+
+so the new key is written into Prime's `providers.json`.
+
+## 6. Disconnecting
+
+```sh
+polli harness prime off
+```
+
+What this does:
+
+1. Backs up `providers.json` and `skills/`.
+2. Removes the `pollinations` entry from `providers.json`.
+3. Removes `skills/polli.md`.
+4. Rotates the `prime-agent`-scoped key.
+
+To keep the key (e.g. you want to reuse it elsewhere):
+
+```sh
+polli harness prime off --keep-key
+```
+
+**Nothing else about your Prime installation changes.** Sessions,
+memories, other skills, and unrelated config are left intact.
+
+## 7. Recovery
+
+Every run (on or off) writes a backup under
+`$PRIME_HOME/.backups/polli-<ts>/`. To restore an earlier state:
+
+```sh
+cp -r ~/.prime/.backups/polli-<ts>/* ~/.prime/
+```
+
+## 8. Troubleshooting
+
+| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |
+---|---|---|
+| `Prime Agent was not found` | No `~/.prime/config.json` | Install Prime, then `polli harness prime on` |
+| `provider: absent` in status | Provider was removed manually | `polli harness prime on` |
+| `skill: absent` in status | Skill was deleted manually | `polli harness prime on` |
+| Auth failures after rotation | Prime still has the old key | `polli harness prime on` |
+| Unknown model error | Stale `--default-model` | The installer falls back to the default automatically; pick from `polli harness prime models` |
+
+## 9. What this integration deliberately does **not** do
+
+* It does **not** install Prime Agent for you. If Prime is missing,
+  you get the official install URL.
+* It does **not** touch Prime's sessions, memories, or unrelated
+  skills.
+* It does **not** register a bespoke Prime MCP server (out of scope
+  for the initial integration).
+* It does **not** issue a key under your default scope; the key is
+  tagged `prime-agent` so it can be rotated independently.
